{"last_node_id":96,"last_link_id":359,"nodes":[{"id":56,"type":"Note","pos":[140,770],"size":[325,80],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Optional: VAE","properties":{"text":""},"widgets_values":["Almost all checkpoints come with a VAE built in so this node is just a backup and can be ignored, but if they don't, or you'd rather use another, you can pick one here."],"color":"#1A1717","bgcolor":"#212121"},{"id":58,"type":"Note","pos":[1200,330],"size":[210,150],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"KSampler","properties":{"text":""},"widgets_values":["KSampler is the special node type in ComfyUI that changes random noise into meaningful images. You can leave these settings as is, or experiment. When you've chosen your options, click \"The triangle/Queue Prompt\" on the right or press the key combo Control - Enter\n"],"color":"#1A1717","bgcolor":"#212121"},{"id":61,"type":"Note","pos":[1730,440],"size":[350,155],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Save Image","properties":{"text":""},"widgets_values":["By default your image will save to /output/ComfyUI####.png. If you prefer something else, be sure to adjust it.\n\nExample:\n\nin a folder /06/ComfyUI\nseed in filename  - /%KSampler.seed%\nsteps - %KSampler.steps%\ncfg - %KSampler.cfg%\nprompt - %CLIPTextEncode.text%\ncheckpoint - %CheckpointLoaderSimple.text%"],"color":"#1A1717","bgcolor":"#212121"},{"id":12,"type":"SaveImage","pos":[1730,640],"size":[350,270],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":27,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"images","type":"IMAGE","link":9}],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["ComfyUI"],"color":"#37323a","bgcolor":"#231e26"},{"id":70,"type":"Note","pos":[140,420],"size":[325,75],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":3,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Welcome!","properties":{"text":""},"widgets_values":["In ComfyUI, boxes called nodes contain the instructions to make everything happen. Begin by choosing a checkpoint from the Load Checkpoint node below!\n"],"color":"#1A1717","bgcolor":"#212121"},{"id":60,"type":"Note","pos":[1210,530],"size":[465,185],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":4,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"More on Ksampler","properties":{"text":""},"widgets_values":["Sampler and scheduler type affect the reproducibility and variation of the image.\n\nCFG controls how strict or relaxed the AI should be when interpreting prompts. Most models fall in the 3-16 CFG range. At the extreme edges of the acceptable range the number often alters brightness, contrast, or color.\n\nSteps determine how the noise is processed. Increasing the number may improve detail, but at some point improvements tend to become less noticeable and more wasteful of processing power. 10-50 steps is the typical value, but always follow the guidelines provided by your checkpoint creator, as there are wide variations.\n\n"],"color":"#1A1717","bgcolor":"#212121"},{"id":59,"type":"Note","pos":[1230,760],"size":[475,275],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"More on Prompts","properties":{"text":""},"widgets_values":["Everyone has a different way of writing prompts, and that's okay! There's no wrong way to make art, but some methods do provide more control and accuracy than others. Here's some tips to get started:\n\nStable Diffusion 1 prompts are lists or tags like:\n\n    honeycomb, bees, hive\n\nStable Diffusion XL prompts are sentences and lists, like:\n\n    A swarm of busy bees working on home improvement, honeycomb, bees, hive\n\nStable Diffusion 3 prompts are more like a book:\n\n    Dressed in plaid, suspenders these handy honeybees are hard at work on their luxurious honeycomb, preparing the gooey, hexagonal home using power tools and table saws. A swarm of busy bees working on home improvement, honeycomb, bees, hive\n\nIf your computer is a bit older or you run into problems, you might have better luck using the SD3-specific workflow."],"color":"#1A1717","bgcolor":"#212121"},{"id":57,"type":"Note","pos":[490,730],"size":[320,160],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":6,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Optional : Empty Latent","properties":{"text":""},"widgets_values":["These numbers generate the canvases of your images, which begin in a miniature form called a latent. The difference in width and height not only changes the size but often the composition as well. Feel free to play with the options of the latent that matches your checkpoint version.\n\nThe 'Batch' option allows you to generate large quantites of images all at once. Be aware that memory use increases with this number, which can cause errors."],"color":"#1A1717","bgcolor":"#212121"},{"id":54,"type":"Note","pos":[830,290],"size":[350,70],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":7,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Prompt Encoders","properties":{"text":""},"widgets_values":["The text encoders accept prompt text and guide the model to focus on your image features. desired ones go in the top node and unwanted ones in the darker one at the bottom."],"color":"#1A1717","bgcolor":"#212121"},{"id":2,"type":"KSampler","pos":[1430,220],"size":[210,262],"flags":{"collapsed":false},"order":25,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"model","type":"MODEL","link":340},{"name":"positive","type":"CONDITIONING","link":351},{"name":"negative","type":"CONDITIONING","link":342,"slot_index":2},{"name":"latent_image","type":"LATENT","link":338,"slot_index":3}],"outputs":[{"name":"LATENT","type":"LATENT","links":[65],"slot_index":0,"shape":3}],"title":"3 KSampler","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"KSampler"},"widgets_values":[426278637500860,"randomize",20,3.4,"dpmpp_2m","karras",1],"color":"#534953","bgcolor":"#3f353f"},{"id":29,"type":"RecourseCkpt","pos":[1170,140],"size":[178,166],"flags":{"collapsed":true},"order":19,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"model_opta","type":"MODEL","link":273,"shape":7